  "term": "olivary nucleus",
  "definition": "The olivary nucleus is a group of nerve cell clusters in the brainstem, in the hindbrain, also called the olivary body. It is part of the medulla oblongata and pontine tegmentum, helps with motor control, and provides major sensory input to the cerebellum.",
